        ├── controllers/
        └── dto/
```

## 40. Cursor Implementation Policy

When modifying POS:

1. Read this rule.
2. Read the POS documentation.
3. Inspect existing bounded contexts.
4. Preserve module boundaries.
5. Implement domain behavior first.
6. Define application ports.
7. Implement infrastructure adapters.
8. Add API endpoints.
9. Add authorization.
10. Add migrations.
11. Add tests.
12. Run architecture checks.
13. Run typecheck.
14. Run lint.
15. Run tests.
16. Run production build.

Do not mark work complete while any required check is failing.

## 41. Priority

When requirements conflict, prioritize:

1. Financial correctness
2. Security
3. Tenant isolation
4. Inventory correctness
5. Data integrity
6. Idempotency
7. Reliability
8. Maintainability
9. Performance
10. Convenience

Never sacrifice correctness for UI speed or implementation convenience.
